course: dictionary
lesson: 11935
title: Big words about choosing people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Candidacy is a formal word. It means putting yourself forward to be chosen, for example in an election or for a job. Its clue is the word candidate: a candidate is the person who stands for something, and a candidacy is the state of being one.
explain: «She announced her candidacy for president.» The words announced and president are clues. People announce things they are serious about, and a president is chosen in an election, so candidacy must mean trying to be chosen.
explain: At school it works the same way. «Sam announced his candidacy for school council.» Sam wants his classmates to vote for him, so his candidacy is his offer to be on the council.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Sam announced his wish to be chosen for school council» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Candidacy means being a candidate in an election, or trying to be chosen for a job or position.
fact: Candidacy is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in news reports, official letters and school elections.
fact: The plural of candidacy is candidacies: the y changes to ies.
fact: In UK English, candidature means the same thing as candidacy.
fact: A candidacy is the act of standing for something; the person who does it is the candidate.
exercise: «Sam announced his candidacy for school council.» What does candidacy mean here? | Writing a letter to the head teacher | *Standing to be chosen for the school council | Cleaning the classroom windows | Winning a game at lunchtime
exercise: Which word is a UK English alternative for candidacy? | candid | *candidature | candle | candy
exercise: «Ben's candidacy for class captain starts on Monday.» What is starting on Monday? | A spelling test | *Ben's bid to be chosen as class captain | A class trip to the zoo | A new reading book
test: «The candidacy was announced on the evening news.» What was announced? | A change to the weather | A new film about animals | *Someone's bid to be chosen in an election | A school trip to the museum
test: Which of these is a candidacy? | *Putting your name forward to be chosen for a job | Losing a game of football | Eating lunch early in the hall | Painting a picture of the sea
exam: What does the formal word candidacy mean? | *Being a candidate who is trying to be chosen in an election or for a job | Being very old and wise | Winning a prize at a fair | Choosing a new pair of shoes
